  "description": "Ohio's 11th Congressional District covers portions of Cuyahoga County, including most of Cleveland and its eastern suburbs. Incumbent Democratic U.S. Representative Shontel Brown, first elected in a 2021 special election, is seeking re-election against Republican nominee Mike Kirchner, a retired consulting actuary and mayor of Jeffersonville. The district is heavily Democratic \u2014 Cook Political Report rates it as Safe Democratic \u2014 and has been represented by Democrats since its creation. The race features a contrast between Brown's record on federal investment and social policy and Kirchner's focus on fiscal conservatism.",
